<title>EGYPT: Egyptian foreign reserves hit all-time high.</title>
<headline>Egyptian foreign reserves hit all-time high.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's net international reserves stood at $19.482 billion at the end of March 1997, a historic high for the end of a month.</p>
<p>The reserves were sharply up on $19.004 billion at the end of February and $18.278 billion at the end of March 1996, according to figures in a Central Bank bulletin.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
